  "sourceUrl": "https://www.alliedtelesis.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/ati-x530series-ds.pdf",
  "notes": "The all-fibre member of the family: 24 SFP slots that take Allied Telesis 100Mbps and 1Gbps SFP modules (ports 1-24) plus 4 x 1/10G SFP+ (ports 25-28, with 27/S1 and 28/S2 the default stacking ports). 128 Gbps fabric and 95 Mpps are lower than on the copper 28-port models because 24 x 1G offers less than 20 x 1G + 4 x 5G. No PoE, no multi-gigabit, no copper at all - a fibre aggregation or long-run access box. 441 x 323 x 44 mm, 5.2 kg, 62 W, 36 dBA. Console is the front-panel RJ-45 RS-232 port (AlliedWare Plus default 9600 8-N-1, no flow control; the switch ships with the manager/friend logins), reached with the RJ-45-to-DB-9 cable in the box or an AT-VT-Kit3 USB-to-serial cable. The management panel also carries a USB port and the eco-friendly button; neither is a network interface, so neither is modelled. Numbers: the x530 Series datasheet SPECIFICATIONS and Power and Noise tables and the model page at https://www.alliedtelesis.com/us/en/products/switches/x530-series; port numbering from the x530 Quick Installation Guide (https://www.alliedtelesis.com/sites/default/files/file/2022-03/ati-x530-english-qig.pdf) and, for the 10/18/28GSX/DP port fronts, the VCStack installation guide (https://www.alliedtelesis.com/sites/default/files/documents/installation-guides/ati_x530_vc_stacking_ig.pdf)."
